From 34aa8bacc0c63d247e177b20490b13e7f9557fdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:12:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/41] tee: qseecom: say why qcom_mdt_load() is not the
 missing piece

Reviewers reasonably ask why a driver handling MDT images does not call the
kernel's existing MDT loader, and the comment asserted a preference without
evidence. Replace it with the reason.

qcom_mdt_load() solves the remoteproc problem: scatter each segment to its
p_paddr inside a carveout. QSEECOM's APP_START takes one contiguous buffer --
the .mdt followed by the segment payloads, with an mdt length and a total
length. Same file format, different contracts.

And for this image the program headers are not usable as a file layout at all.
Checked against Goodix gfenu: segment 0 declares p_offset 0, which would
overwrite the ELF and program headers being parsed, and segments 6 and 7
declare the same p_offset *and* the same p_paddr with different sizes, so
placing by p_offset makes one overwrite the other. Concatenation in
program-header order is what the vendor's loader does and what TZ accepts.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
index f8d6eb772..836c7f239 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
@@ -1195,6 +1195,20 @@ static void qseecom_tee_supp_release(struct tee_context *ctx)
  * .bNN in program-header order -- is firmware layout policy, and it belongs in
  * user space with the rest of it.
  *
+ * qcom_mdt_load() is not the missing piece here, despite handling the same
+ * file format. It solves the remoteproc problem: scatter each segment to its
+ * p_paddr inside a carveout. QSEECOM's APP_START instead takes one contiguous
+ * buffer -- the .mdt followed by the segment payloads, with an mdt length and a
+ * total length -- so the two want different things from the same files.
+ *
+ * The program headers cannot even be read as a file layout for this image.
+ * Taking a real one (Goodix gfenu): segment 0 has p_offset 0, which would
+ * overwrite the very ELF and program headers being parsed, and segments 6 and 7
+ * declare the same p_offset and the same p_paddr with different sizes, so
+ * placing by p_offset makes one overwrite the other. Concatenation in
+ * program-header order is what the vendor's own loader does, and it is what
+ * produces an image TZ accepts.
+ *
